        - MEDIUM [APPLIED 2026-04-29]: name the Wald failure regimes precisely
            - Current text: "Don't use Wald near boundaries. Don't use Wald at small N, period." This is correct but vague. Sharper version: Wald is unreliable when N * p_hat < 5 or N * (1 - p_hat) < 5, and is degenerate (collapses to a single point) when p_hat is exactly 0 or 1.
            - Edit Loop B "Rule of thumb" to give the n*p_hat heuristic.
